[00:10.76]Did the boy go where he wanted to? | 那个男孩到达了目的地吗？
[00:15.41]Children who play truant from school are unimaginative. | 逃学的孩子们都缺乏想象力。
[00:20.83]A quiet days' fishing, | 他们通常能够做到的，
[00:22.88]or eight hours in a cinema seeing the same film over and over again, is usually as far as they get. | 至多是安安静静地钓一天鱼，或在电影院里坐上8个小时，一遍遍地看同一部电影。
[00:32.68]They have all been put to shame by a boy who, while playing truant travelled 1, 600 miles. | 有一个男孩在逃学期间旅行了1,600英里，使所有逃学的孩子都相形见绌。
[00:42.90]He hitchhiked to Dover and towards evening went into a boat to find somewhere to sleep. | 他搭便车到了多佛，傍晚时分钻进了一条船，想找个地方睡觉。
[00:51.32]When he woke up next morning, he discovered that the boat had, in the meantime, travelled to Calais. | 第二天早上他醒来时，发现那条船在这段时间里已经到了加来。
[01:00.90]No one noticed the boy as he crept off. | 谁也没有发现那个男孩溜下船。
[01:04.89]From there, he hitchhiked to Paris in a lorry. | 他从那里搭上一辆卡车到了巴黎。
[01:09.46]The driver gave him a few biscuits and a cup of coffee and left him just outside the city. | 司机给了他几块饼干和一杯咖啡，把他留在了巴黎城外。
[01:18.09]The next car the boy stopped did not take him into the centre of Paris as he hoped it would, | 男孩拦住的下一辆车并没有像他希望的那样把他带到巴黎市中心，
[01:26.40]but to Perpignan on the French-Spanish border. | 而是把他送到了法西边境的佩皮尼昂。
[01:31.54]There he was picked up by a policeman and sent back to England by the local authorities. | 在那里他被一名警察截住，由当地政府送回了英国。
[01:39.10]He has surely set up a record for the thousands of children who dream of evading school. | 他无疑为成千上万梦想逃学的孩子们创了一项纪录。
